   "text": "The vase is modeled, but the design check failed two items, so I've stopped there and not called it done.\n\n- **Overall size:** the plan expected 80 x 69.28 x 160 mm, but the part is 80 x 80 x 160 mm. The 69.28 figure was my mistake. A hexagon turned through its twist has corners that reach 40 mm on Y at intermediate heights, so the true footprint is 80 x 80 mm. The geometry matches your request.\n- **Minimum wall:** the checker could not measure it because the part is too dense for that test. The walls are built at 2 mm by the shell step, which is well above the 0.8 mm minimum for a 0.4 mm nozzle.\n\nThe model has three steps: a smooth 5-section loft with the 60 degree twist, a 2 mm shell with the top open, and a 3 mm solid hexagon floor. It is closed and watertight.\n\nDo you want me to keep the 80 x 80 mm footprint and update the plan to match? I can then re-run the check and, if you approve, slice it for the P1S in PLA. Nothing has been sliced or sent to a printer."
